# hosts/asus-tuf-a15.env — the machine this repo is developed on.
#
# ASUS TUF Gaming A15 (FA507NV), Ryzen 5 7535HS + RTX 4060 Mobile. Matched
# on DMI product_name by scripts/host-profile.sh. Loaded on top of
# default.env, so it only has to state what differs.
#
# ── Why the idle ladder is off here, explicitly ─────────────────────────
# It is already off in practice: this machine's battery does not register
# at all (/sys/class/power_supply holds an ACAD adapter and no BAT*), so
# default.env's IDLE_REQUIRE_BATTERY guard blocks every action. That is an
# accident of the current hardware state, not a decision, and it is worth
# exactly nothing the day a working battery goes back in -- at which point
# this machine would start dimming, locking and, at the 30-minute rung,
# SUSPENDING itself, with no change made to any config to cause it.
#
# That last one is not a cosmetic risk on this machine. It is hand-managed
# around a fault where the CPU dropping below a certain frequency crashes
# it into a reboot (idle=poll, a 2.5 GHz floor and a pinned governor, all
# outside this repo), and a suspend/resume cycle is the least tested path
# through exactly that machinery. It is not something to have triggered by
# a timer, from a config nobody re-read, because a battery was replaced.
#
# So the refusal is stated as identity rather than inferred from hardware:
# this machine, by name, does not idle. Remove the line and you get the
# default laptop ladder -- which is the right thing on a laptop and the
# wrong thing here.
IDLE_ENABLED=0
